            <semantic:sequenceFlow id="_8703e51d-ebc1-4788-9ca4-e67e09909865" triso:readOnly="false" sourceRef="_73f1326b-1a9f-40a0-87d5-ccb67be3ffb1" targetRef="_3bd39776-8424-4a12-ad66-83e0fb26bfea"/>
            <semantic:sequenceFlow id="_1c163328-45c1-4c98-b449-15f95ea2f220" triso:readOnly="false" sourceRef="_3bd39776-8424-4a12-ad66-83e0fb26bfea" targetRef="_448ae137-04a1-4c3f-9849-0221544cb564"/>
            <semantic:sequenceFlow id="_6b8a2fed-986d-4673-a8ec-5540f3655f24" triso:readOnly="false" sourceRef="_448ae137-04a1-4c3f-9849-0221544cb564" targetRef="_f4d2ee51-cf22-44f0-b76c-d60cbf94daca"/>
            <semantic:sequenceFlow id="_e8a2ee64-5e29-45eb-8f92-1b617ad4558b" triso:readOnly="false" sourceRef="_f4d2ee51-cf22-44f0-b76c-d60cbf94daca" targetRef="_7c679f04-1a7a-4f4c-9360-89f1aba89d97"/>
            <semantic:textAnnotation id="_ba94b5b3-95b0-4c82-a0ef-26d46fbd85f3">
                <semantic:text>The Inclusive split allows one, two, or all three branches to activate, depending on the request.</semantic:text>
            </semantic:textAnnotation>
            <semantic:textAnnotation id="_ee15b3be-4d30-48e0-a927-0c6dcd9ccc45">
                <semantic:text>Once the needed repair subprocesses are complete, the Inclusive join brings the flow back together. Unlike a parallel join, it waits only for the branches that were activated by the split.</semantic:text>
            </semantic:textAnnotation>
            <semantic:textAnnotation id="_92c4aeb4-dce1-446e-9741-9ce4aafb4c15">
                <semantic:text>Why Inclusive Split/Join Fits Best
Not every request requires every branch. A broken sink doesn’t need an electrician; flickering lights don’t need a carpenter.
Some requests require multiple trades. For example, a water-damaged ceiling may need plumbing + carpentry.
The Inclusive Gateway split handles both cases, and the join ensures the process completes only after the right combination of work is finished.</semantic:text>
            </semantic:textAnnotation>
        </semantic:subProcess>
        <semantic:endEvent id="_f38e7158-e19f-4174-9e8e-1f1d54dc47be" name="Repair completed" triso:readOnly="false">
